## db access
- you need first to start docker 
- specify the in docker-compose the info for the service you need to use for example posgresql
- you need to specify in the application.properties which db properties to use
- create in resources/sql/migration an initial DB which the first thing runs 
- to check directly in the db open the container in docker deskop then run the terminal and the run psql -U noviq -d noviq after that you can run whatever you want in the db 
- to list the tables use : \dt
- when finished just use \q
- if you change the initial schema you will need to stop using docker compose down -v to remove the volumes as well and start the container one more time because Flyway uses version to compare and update the schema.


## Security
- you need to go export a JWT_SECRET, for example export JWT_SECRET="THIS_IS_MY_SUPER_SECRET_KEY_12345678901234567890" this is going to be used in order to create and sign the tokens for every request I have already gave it a fallback if it is not set